From 1d5c3216e4f74b8e94e2c8f33fb6e1527e94d057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:49:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/43] Resident geometry: admit on the second sighting, evict
 the oldest

The entry table filled and reset itself (every entry dropped, the whole
scene rebuilt) every ~25 s of play. The keys that kept arriving were
post-processing quads (tone map, bloom and blur chain) drawn from a
streaming vertex ring whose offset moves on every draw: a new key each
time, about 1,000 before the ring wraps, on pages written too often to
watch, and each left a "dynamic" placeholder behind.

- No placeholder for a draw whose memory cannot be watched; the attempt
  fails fast next time (vm_watch knows the page).
- Admission: an entry is made on a key's second sighting. First
  sightings live in a fixed direct-mapped filter (ENG_GEOM_SEEN, 4096
  keys), so one-off keys never take a slot or GPU memory.
- Eviction instead of a reset: out of slots or GPU memory, the entries
  drawn longest ago go, a quarter at a time, never one drawn in the last
  ENG_GEOM_MIN_AGE (120) frames; still no room, new entries wait
  ENG_GEOM_NOROOM_WAIT frames rather than retrying every draw. Erase is
  backward-shift deletion; a rebuilt or retired entry gives its GPU
  memory back.
- Backend: geom_reset becomes geom_release. The Vulkan arena hands out
  power-of-two blocks from 256 bytes; a released block waits until an
  allocation that finds no room has waited for the GPU, then serves any
  request its size or smaller. Handles are recycled.
- RSX_GEOM_CACHE_STATS reports admissions, first sightings, evictions,
  no-room, entries and MB; RSX_GEOM_CACHE_LOG=<n> logs the draws that make
  entries with every part of their key; RSX_GEOM_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES and
  RSX_GEOM_ARENA_CHUNKS shrink the cache to test eviction.

Five-minute soaks (walking, menu, map, guard, sword): the table levels
off at ~1,200-1,450 entries / 73-76 MB, 86-88% of draws resident, no
eviction or reset needed; 59.5-60 fps, p99 21-22 ms. Shrunk to 1,100
entries / 128 MB it evicts old entries and keeps 88% of draws resident.
The check mode found no missed write in nine runs.
